  "id": "Compound::DB00603 - Gene::2908",
  "verbalization": "Medroxyprogesterone Acetate is implicated in the regulation of Nr3c1 through a series of interconnected pathways involving corticosteroids and hormone therapy agents. The evidence suggests that Medroxyprogesterone Acetate, as a corticosteroid, can cause the development of conditions such as Cleft Palate and Meningioma, which in turn bind to Nr3c1. This indicates a potential mechanism where Medroxyprogesterone Acetate, through its role as a corticosteroid, influences the expression or activity of Nr3c1 via downstream pathways involving hormone therapy agents and therapeutic steroids. The shared involvement of Acetate Ester and Hormone Therapy Agent as common ancestors further supports a unified mechanism, where Medroxyprogesterone Acetate exerts its effects through a common pathway that ultimately leads to Nr3c1 binding. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Medroxyprogesterone Acetate in modulating Nr3c1 through hormonal and steroid-mediated mechanisms.",
